# Cloudflare Pages header rules. The build copies this file into dist/, and Pages applies its rules
# instead of serving it as a file (PLAN.md Decision 11). Pages itself already sends nosniff and a
# Referrer-Policy.
#
# Every response gets HSTS, at 300 seconds until it is raised in steps, and a CSP that only keeps
# other origins from framing the site and allows no <object> or <base>. It has no script-src or
# style-src: the head scripts are inline, production also loads the zone's analytics beacon, and
# the examples use style="".
#
# Caching: no two rules set Cache-Control on one path. The site's CSS and JavaScript and vendored
# femto keep 5 minutes, so the next pages of a visit reuse them without asking, and a deploy reaches
# a returning reader within those 5 minutes. The fonts, the .woff2 files in /assets/fonts/, keep a
# year: they are pinned files whose names never change, so a changed font needs a new file name, and
# its @font-face rule a new url(). Everything else, OFL.txt beside them included, keeps Pages'
# default, "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", so a deploy shows at once.
#
# Markdown (PLAN.md Decision 19): the zone answers /docs with /docs.md's body when the request's
# Accept names text/markdown, so both vary on Accept. /docs also names /docs.md in a Link header, for
# a client that reads headers and not the page's head. No rule sets a Content-Type: Pages types .md
# files itself, and a rule's type would also reach the 404 page under its path.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'

/docs
  Vary: Accept
  Link: </docs.md>; rel="alternate"; type="text/markdown"

/docs.md
  Vary: Accept

/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/vendor/femto/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/assets/fonts/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
